-- 1. user = currentUser() matches only the caller's own rows, and the KILL statement itself is excluded; with the dedicated user idle otherwise, the match is empty and the default throws
throws NOTHING_TO_KILL
-- 2. the same empty match with the setting off
no rows, no error
-- 3. TEST is a dry run: an empty match is an empty preview, not an exception
empty preview
-- 4. killing a live query must not throw with the default setting and must stop it
rows: 1
victim: gone
-- 5. KILL MUTATION with an empty match throws by default
throws NOTHING_TO_KILL
-- 6. the same empty match with the setting off
no rows, no error
-- 7. KILL MUTATION TEST with nothing to kill is an empty preview
empty preview
